{"t_ms": 707937, "conversation_id": "v2llm_streaming_retrieve_s029", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n", "Lost & Found Policy\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nItems found within the hotel premises are recorded and securely stored by the housekeeping department. Guests who believe they have misplaced personal belongings should contact the Front Desk with a detailed description of the item. Unclaimed items are generally retained for 90 days before being disposed of in accordance with hotel policy.", "Vegetarian & Vegan Options\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nThe hotel offers a variety of vegetarian and vegan dishes across all dining outlets. Guests can choose from salads, soups, plant-based curries, pasta, rice bowls, and dairy-free desserts. Customized vegan meals can also be prepared upon request. Please inform the restaurant staff of your dietary preferences before ordering."], "scores": [1.0481476783752441, 1.1616840362548828, 1.1685359477996826], "filenames": ["README.md", "09_lost_and_found.txt", "29_vegan_menu.txt"], "timing_policy": "sentence_end", "timing_trigger": "sentence_end", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_